    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187-a1">

                <pb facs="0574" n="539" xml:id="pg539"/>


                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1973-10-16">October 16,
                        1973</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">SUMMARY OF DECISIONS</p>
                <p>The Secretary decided:</p>
                <p>p. 4, 5 1. That we should <hi rendition="#italic">begin negotiations with the
                        Portuguese on the Azores Bases</hi> and also <hi rendition="#italic">inform
                        them of PL–480] grain</hi> we are providing.</p>
                <p>p. 10, 11 2. That <hi rendition="#italic">Marshall Wright should inform key
                        Members</hi> of both the House and Senate <hi rendition="#italic">of the
                        relationship between the resupply of Israel and our relations with
                        Portugal.</hi></p>
                <p>p. 14, 15 3. That we should make <hi rendition="#italic">strong statements</hi>
                    at a high level <hi rendition="#italic">to our NATO allies</hi> on the Middle East situation specifically
                    asking them <hi rendition="#italic">whether they think it is in their interest
                        to encourage an adventurist Soviet foreign policy.</hi></p>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to the Middle East.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Thomas R. Pickering <lb/>
                        <affiliation><title>Executive Secretary</title></affiliation>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
